      madhyamaka: 'Yā Tathāgatasya svabhāvā sā jagataḥ svabhāvā (Tathāgata\'s essence = world\'s essence). Tathāgata niḥsvabhāva (Tathāgata has no essence). Jagat niḥsvabhāva (world without essence). The syllogism establishes universal emptiness.',
